Package: bottom.UpR
Type: Package
Title: Bayesian Bottom-Up Population Modelling with INLA-SPDE
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Chibuzor Christopher", "Nnanatu",
           email = "94153331+ChibuzorNnanatu@users.noreply.github.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Andrew J", "Tatem", role = "aut")
    )
Description: Generic Bayesian bottom-up population modelling for population counts and people-per-building responses. Supports automatic response-type detection and compatible likelihood selection among Gamma and lognormal models for people-per-building responses, and Poisson and negative binomial models for count responses. Spatial structure is represented through the INLA-SPDE framework; hierarchical effects are optional and user-adaptable; cross-validation supports random, spatial-block, grouped region/source holdouts; and chunked joint-posterior prediction supports fine-grid population surfaces and draw-wise administrative aggregation without double-counting building exposure.
